mrpt (1:3.1.2+ds-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream version 3.1.2+ds
  * Remove debian/patches already integrated upstream
  * debian/control: python3-mrpt-core Breaks/Replaces python3-pymrpt,
    the monolithic MRPT 2.x Python package superseded by the per-module
    python3-mrpt-* packages. Its leftover mrpt/__init__.py would
    otherwise turn the mrpt namespace package into a regular one and
    hide modules installed elsewhere.
  * Add libmrpt-imgui-vendor-dev: static archive, headers and CMake
    config of the new mrpt_imgui_vendor module (vendored Dear ImGui
    docking branch, ImPlot, portable-file-dialogs and
    IconFontCppHeaders). Static by design, since Dear ImGui has no
    SOVERSION nor ABI stability promise. Required by
    find_package(mrpt_imgui).
  * debian/copyright: document the sources vendored by mrpt_imgui_vendor
    and its embedded Material Symbols font subset, and repack out
    imgui's prebuilt Windows GLFW libraries and unused bundled TTF
    fonts.

 -- Jose Luis Blanco Claraco <joseluisblancoc@gmail.com>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 10:41:12 +0200

mrpt (1:3.0.5+ds-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream version 3.0.5+ds
  * debian/patches: remove now obsolete patches
  * debian: port packaging to MRPT 3.x modular colcon build
  * debian/tests/control: ship an explicit autopkgtest overriding autodep8's
    auto-generated python3 test. autodep8 derives the import name from the
    binary package name ("python3-mrpt-bayes" -> "import mrpt_bayes"), which
    never works: the pybind11 extensions install as the "mrpt" namespace
    package, so the real import is "import mrpt.bayes".
  * debian/control: drop redundant Priority field (defaults to optional),
    drop redundant Rules-Requires-Root: no field (now the dpkg default), and
    bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4 (no changes needed)
  * Remove the prebuilt test binary modules/mrpt_img/tests/generate_test_data
    from the source tree and keep it listed in debian/copyright Files-Excluded
    (fixes source-contains-prebuilt-binary and source-ships-excluded-file)
  * debian/control: add python3-numpy to the runtime Depends of
    python3-mrpt-math and python3-mrpt-img. Their __init__.py modules do a
    top-level "import numpy"
  * debian/control: make each python3-mrpt-* package directly depend on every
    sibling module its __init__.py imports at load time.
  * debian/rules: wrap the colcon build in "setarch -R" (ADDR_NO_RANDOMIZE)
    for reproducibility. Without it, ASLR-seeded GCC DWARF location-list
    emission made .debug_info/.debug_loclists -- and hence the GNU build-id --
    differ run-to-run despite an identical source tree, build path and -j,
    breaking debrebuild.
  * debian/control: fix not-binnmuable-all-depends-any on libmrpt-dev by
    replacing the strict (= ${source:Version}) pin on its arch:any -dev
    dependencies with a (>= ${source:Version}), (<< ${source:Version}.1~)
    range, as recommended by lintian
  * debian/copyright: update cmake module file patterns to their new
    per-module paths, and drop entries for files removed upstream
  * debian/copyright: normalize license stanza formatting and use the
    canonical "Expat" identifier instead of "MIT"
  * debian/rules: remove now obsolete -D cmake symbols
  * debian/rules: enable unit tests via "colcon test" under xvfb-run, with
    verbose console output, failing the build on test failures
  * debian/control: add xvfb and xauth build dependencies for running the
    test suite headlessly
  * debian/rules: pass -DBUILD_TESTING=ON to colcon's cmake-args; without
    it no test binaries/registrations are generated and colcon test-result
    reports "0 tests"
  * debian/rules: export PYTHONPATH/LD_LIBRARY_PATH pointing at the merged
    colcon install tree when running colcon test, fixing Python binding
    tests
  * debian/rules: drop optimize=+lto from DEB_BUILD_MAINT_OPTIONS; GCC's LTO
    miscompiles exception unwinding across thread boundaries here, causing
    spurious test crashes in mrpt_maps and mrpt_nav
  * debian/control, debian/copyright: unembed exprtk.hpp, building against
    the system libexprtk-dev (Closes: #1094437)
  * debian/patches: add 0001-Fix-ambiguous-operator-on-i386-array_string-string_
    fixing an i386-only FTBFS in mrpt_typemeta's test suite for platforms
    where ptrdiff_t==int

 -- Jose Luis Blanco Claraco <joseluisblancoc@gmail.com>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 20:59:42 +0200

